{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/3224","id":3595808839,"node_id":"PR_kwDOEFLz887WU7BH","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3224","diff_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3224.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3224.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/3224","number":3224,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"state: fix HA tracking losing secondary after all routers offline","user":{"login":"kradalby","id":98431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby","html_url":"https://github.com/kradalby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"When all subnet routers serving a prefix go offline simultaneously and one returns, headscale could end up with the returning node marked online in `NodeStore` but absent from `PrimaryRoutes` for the prefix, with HA tracking stuck until daemon restart.\n\nThe generation counter added in b09af384 closed the obvious window but left the gen check non-atomic with the subsequent `NodeStore.UpdateNode` and `PrimaryRoutes.SetRoutes` calls. A concurrent `Connect` that bumped the counter and rewrote primary routes could be silently overtaken by a stale `Disconnect`'s `SetRoutes(empty)`. The grace-period flow in `poll.go` hides this on most cable-pull cadences, which is why three earlier reproductions (servertest graceful, integration graceful, integration cable-pull-via-iptables) all pass on main.\n\nReplace the standalone counter with a per-node `nodeLock` pairing the gen counter and a mutex. `Connect` and `Disconnect` now run under the lock and re-check gen inside the critical section, making gen evaluation and the mutations atomic. Per-node so unrelated nodes never contend; same-node steady state has effectively no contention.\n\n`TestConnectDisconnectRace` drives the race directly through `State`, fails deterministically on main, and passes under the lock. The earlier servertest, integration and cable-pull reproductions stay as regression coverage for the user-reported sequence. A property test on `PrimaryRoutes` joins as a safety net for future changes to primary route selection.\n\nFixes #3203\n\n> Generated with the help of an AI assistant","created_at":"2026-04-28T12:17:31Z","updated_at":"2026-04-29T17:08:40Z","closed_at":"2026-04-29T17:08:40Z","merged_at":"2026-04-29T17:08:40Z","merge_commit_sha":"3d5c0af4e703482aff8f979ff5bde330a7bf97f5","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"ohdearaugustin","id":14001491,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MDAxNDkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14001491?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohdearaugustin","html_url":"https://github.com/ohdearaugustin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohdearaugustin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohdearaugustin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohdearaugustin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohdearaugustin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohdearaugustin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohdearaugustin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.